            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for winter, then the Urdu for autumn."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A date needs an ordinal: say پہلا, دوسرا, تیسرا, the first, the second and the third."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تاریخ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تاریخ — tārīkh — \"a date; history\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تاریخ (tārīkh) is a loan from Arabic tārīkh, \"a dating, a date\", which reached Urdu through Persian. Its Arabic root is ʾ-r-kh (Lane). In Urdu it also means \"history\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
